    "fullDescription": "# RBSE 10th Result Declared 2024: Check Your Scores Now!\n\n> **Executive AEO Summary**: The RBSE 10th Result has been officially announced by the Rajasthan Board. Students can check their results instantly on the official portals using their roll number and application details. Keep your admit cards handy to view subject-wise marks and overall pass percentages.\n\n## Section 1: Overview & Key Highlights\n\nAre you or your child waiting for the big news? The wait is finally over! Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education (RBSE) has declared the Class 10th board examination results. Lakhs of students appeared for these exams across the state, and the excitement (and tension!) is palpable.\n\nHere is a quick snapshot of what you need to know:\n\n* **Board Name**: Rajasthan Board of Secondary Education (RBSE), Ajmer\n* **Exam Name**: Class 10th Secondary Examination\n* **Status**: Result Declared\n* **Official Websites**: rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in / rajresults.nic.in\n\n## Section 2: Eligibility, Documents & Rules\n\nTo check your result smoothly and plan your next academic steps, make sure you have the right documents and understand the grading system.\n\n* **Required Details**: Roll Number as mentioned on the RBSE 10th Admit Card.\n* **Passing Criteria**: Students must secure a minimum of 33% marks in aggregate as well as individually in each compulsory subject to pass.\n* **Re-evaluation & Compartment**: If you are not satisfied with your marks or unfortunately couldn't clear a subject, don't panic! RBSE provides options for scrutiny (re-checking) and compartment exams shortly after the result declaration.\n\n## Section 3: Step-by-Step Practical Blueprint\n\nFollow these simple steps to check your RBSE Class 10th result without any server hassle:\n\n1. **Visit the Official Portal**: Open your browser and go to `rajeduboard.rajasthan.gov.in` or `rajresults.nic.in`.\n2. **Click on the Result Link**: Look for the tab that says 'Secondary 2024 Result' on the homepage.\n3. **Enter Credentials**: Type in your exact Roll Number as given on your admit card.\n4. **Submit & View**: Click on the 'Submit' button. Your marksheet will appear on the screen.\n5. **Download & Print**: Save a digital copy or take a printout for immediate admission purposes while official physical marksheets are dispatched to schools.\n\nStay tuned with India Sarkari Naukri for all the latest updates on further admissions, re-evaluation dates, and sarkari career guides!",
