    "fullContent": "### Appointment Order In accordance with **Article 280(1)** of the Constitution of India, the President has officially appointed **Dr. Arvind Subramanian**, former Chief Economic Adviser (CEA) to the Government of India, as the **Chairman of the 17th Finance Commission**. ### Composition & Terms of Reference (ToR) Along with the Chairman, four full-time members representing fiscal policy, state administration, and public finance have been notified. Key terms of reference include: 1. **Vertical & Horizontal Devolution:** Determining the percentage share of net proceeds of taxes shared between the Union and States (Vertical), and distribution among States (Horizontal). 2. **Disaster Finance Review:** Re-evaluating funding arrangements for disaster management funds under the Disaster Management Act, 2005. 3. **Local Body Grants:** Formulating performance-linked grant mechanisms for Panchayati Raj Institutions (PRIs) and Urban Local Bodies (ULBs). ### Timeline The 17th Finance Commission has been given a window until October 31, 2027, to submit its final report, which will govern financial devolution for the five-year period spanning **2027-28 to 2031-32**. ### Exam Relevance * **Polity & Economy (Article 280):** Quasi-judicial body constituted every five years. * **Historical Context:** 15th FC was headed by N.K. Singh; 16th FC was headed by Dr. Arvind Panagariya.",
